test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T17:42:42.7853343Z             "body": "This draft preserves the original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging, lifecycle controls and fork-specific installation. Publishing remains disabled. It is not release-ready.\n\nThe journal revalidates schema version/project/key identity under the existing write lock, preventing three reproduced second-connection races from accepting a future/cleared schema version or missing project marker. All12 actual race checks pass across four native component lanes. This is a scoped integrity fix, not a claimed cause/fix for historical initialization timeouts.\n\nCurrent candidate6884c4a shares the tested Ubuntu mirror correction across all five Linux host browser-install job paths and adds failure-only large-DOM call timings. The core masks normalization errors as reference-not-found; timings help distinguish a stale reference from a call interrupted by the test deadline. No extra RPC, wait, retry, default transport or timeout change. Bash/YAML/actionlint and typecheck pass; original Chromium/Firefox large-DOM cases2/2 pass locally. Fresh production install passes;297-file package excludes QA fixtures/actions/evidence. Shellcheck/pyflakes are disabled in actionlint.\n\n[Native91 batch](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39813834089) at74497b1 reports1624 pass/4 fail; [original](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39813834126)570/11. Completed summaries2194/15, reported test skips/cancels0. All five package steps and all four component lanes pass. Linux main207/211/211 pass; Mac210/1, Windows200/3. All17 logs recovered, with one partial EOF retained plus successful ordinary retry. No aggregate cancellation requested.\n\nActual Codex1k passes Linux36.389s/Windows38.721s, model0/owned0. Mac actual times out958 with result available, operatorAttentionfalse, forcedfalse/terminated/removed; sync stdio times out969 with cleanup confirmed. Separate Mac1k transport controls pass. Windows private/inherited/protocol-headed/stock-headed controls also fail this sample, retaining zero-owned audits without relabeling failed actions/cleanup as success. Historical Windows CRASHED750 and native87/136/142 ownership uncertainties remain unresolved.\n\nOriginal failures include Mac screenshot capture and Firefox deadlines, Windows Firefox trace timeout and WebKit WAV/VP9 readiness.11/12 traces and12/12 PDF behaviors pass. Mac Chrome/Chromium/WebKit strict video cases pass; actual-gray gate is ineligible, so no fresh gray-frame controls/independent decoder measurement run. Native90 gray cause remains unresolved; no speculative encoder patch or assertion waiver. Media Foundation already reported installed successfully on Windows.\n\nThree native91 Linux batch lanes each changed one targeted apt source file, left no matched Azure URI, and installed dependencies in80/67/56s. This does not establish a general timing guarantee. Shared preparation for other Linux jobs awaits native92. Final raw checkpoints25..200 and bootstrap phases are retained; API exposes phases plus25..175. Full rows, partial reads and scoped limitations are in docs/evidence/native91-summary.json and leading reports.\n\nG00–G18 in docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md remain authoritative. No merge, publication, unsafe replay, role-based PID filtering or ownership-debt clearance.",
